# 13. Ruby and Ruby on Rails

This is probably the most important thing to know about Ruby's practical history.

**Ruby on Rails**, usually called **Rails**, is a web application framework written in Ruby.

The relationship is:

```text
Ruby
  │
  └── programming language
          │
          ▼
     Ruby on Rails
          │
          └── web framework
```

Rails appeared in the mid-2000s and became one of the most influential web frameworks of its time.

It helped popularize the idea:

> **Convention over configuration**

Instead of configuring everything manually, Rails makes reasonable assumptions for you.

---

# 14. Rails and MVC

Rails uses the **MVC architecture**:

```text
              Browser
                 │
                 ▼
            Controller
             /       \
            /         \
           ▼           ▼
        Model       View
           │           │
           ▼           ▼
       Database      HTML
```

For example:

```text
GET /students/10
        │
        ▼
StudentsController
        │
        ▼
Student model
        │
        ▼
Database
        │
        ▼
View
        │
        ▼
HTML response
```

Rails made this kind of web development extremely productive.

---

# 15. Ruby on Rails' famous philosophy

Rails is associated with several major ideas.

### Convention over configuration

Instead of configuring everything:

```text
"Tell me every detail."
```

Rails says:

```text
"I'll use sensible conventions."
```

### Don't Repeat Yourself

**DRY**:

> Don't Repeat Yourself.

If information can be expressed once, don't unnecessarily duplicate it.

### RESTful design

Rails strongly embraced REST-style web application design.

For example:

```text
GET    /students
POST   /students
GET    /students/1
PATCH  /students/1
DELETE /students/1
```

This should look familiar given your recent study of REST APIs.

