# 18. Ruby vs Python

Ruby and Python are often compared because both became popular general-purpose scripting languages.

|                     | Ruby                 | Python                   |
| ------------------- | -------------------- | ------------------------ |
| Main philosophy     | Programmer happiness | Readability / simplicity |
| Typing              | Dynamic              | Dynamic                  |
| OOP                 | Very strong          | Strong                   |
| Functional features | Strong               | Strong                   |
| Blocks              | Central feature      | No direct equivalent     |
| Web                 | Rails                | Django, Flask, FastAPI   |
| Data science        | Smaller ecosystem    | Extremely strong         |
| AI/ML               | Smaller              | Dominant                 |
| Metaprogramming     | Very powerful        | Powerful                 |
| Syntax              | Flexible             | More standardized        |

A useful conceptual distinction:

```text
Ruby
  ↓
Object-oriented + expressive + metaprogramming
  ↓
Rails
  ↓
Web development
```

while:

```text
Python
  ↓
General-purpose + scientific/data ecosystem
  ↓
NumPy / pandas / PyTorch / TensorFlow
  ↓
AI / ML / Data Science
```

