### The key idea

If **C** represents the **systems-programming tradition**, **Java** represents the **enterprise/JVM tradition**, and **Python** represents the modern **general-purpose/data/AI scripting tradition**, then **Ruby represents the expressive, programmer-productivity-oriented scripting/web tradition**, with **Ruby on Rails** being its most historically important application.

For your Java-backend study, Ruby is also useful to learn conceptually because **Rails and Spring Boot represent two different answers to the same problem: how to make web application development productive**.
